{-
   A join with more than 255 predecessors (J182). `LowerInst::usedCount` was a U8, and a phi has one
   operand per predecessor, so the value `code` answers - a `match` of 260 string arms, each arm its
   own way into the join - wrapped the count and read its alternatives from the wrong place: an
   assertion in a checked build and a wrong answer in a release one. The count is twelve bits now.

   The fixture is generated rather than written, and is only its width: `w0` to `w259`, each
   answering `i * 7 % 13`, and ten words that match nothing.
-}

fn code(word: String) -> Int = match word:
    "w0" -> 0
    "w1" -> 7
    "w2" -> 1
    "w3" -> 8
    "w4" -> 2
    "w5" -> 9
    "w6" -> 3
    "w7" -> 10
    "w8" -> 4
    "w9" -> 11
    "w10" -> 5
    "w11" -> 12
